{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce9MiN8eGB36yPASB6Fv4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That is not something in this repo, so here is what I know from general knowledge — with the caveat that transit details change and mine may be stale.\n\n**Eastgate Park-and-Ride (Bellevue, Washington)**\n- Location: Eastgate area of Bellevue, at the I-90 / 142nd Place SE interchange, next to Bellevue College.\n- Structure: a multi-level parking garage replaced the older surface lot. It is one of King County Metro's largest park-and-ride facilities, with roughly 1,600 stalls. Treat that count as approximate.\n- Transit access: an I-90 freeway station with direct-access ramps lets buses enter and exit without using the general-purpose lanes. Metro and Sound Transit routes serve it, including trans-lake service to Seattle and Issaquah-area service. I am not confident about the current route numbers — Sound Transit restructured East Link feeder service, and route assignments have changed.\n- Typical use: it fills early on weekday mornings.\n\nTwo things I cannot confirm without checking: the exact stall count, and which routes serve it today.\n\nIf you mean a different Eastgate — Cincinnati, Ohio, and other cities also have one — tell me which. I can also run a web search to get current stall counts, hours, permit rules, and routes if that is useful."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15274,"cache_read_input_tokens":18951,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15274},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"510868d1-ea01-444d-908c-8b0331f9ffcd","uuid":"cb4417bc-6d08-433c-bb75-f6402539120b","timestamp":"2026-08-18T01:37:35.161Z","request_id":"req_011Ce9MiMNkcfFRWfv9SKaa3"}
